                        "entry_id": "6dc1f229-1f14-321b-85eb-a2ea47bd92bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who carries out an inspection; an inspector."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "nonstandard"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c23a9dc0-d951-4f9b-8fc9-ce77a804cc6c",
                                "sense_id": "c0019ee3-3024-3f19-a1e4-577a2198cc0a",
                                "text": "Javert was the very incarnation of devotion to duty, fictionally, but he was an unstable character compared to some of our inspectioneers in government."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c793a5e-09c5-4617-b016-67a87f89c5cb",
                                "sense_id": "c0019ee3-3024-3f19-a1e4-577a2198cc0a",
                                "text": "But linguistic “inspectioneers” who take the trouble of comparing Murray and Bradley's account of the word with that of Webster must wonder why the latter ignored or refused to follow the New English Dictionary's lead."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
